cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use enrich in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "enrich: zero-config log line enrichment for Go"
abstract: >-
  enrich is a Go library that auto-detects the format of a log line (JSON,
  logfmt, or one of 20+ plain-text formats such as nginx, klog and syslog) and
  extracts its timestamp, its level normalized to OpenTelemetry's severity
  scale, the message, W3C trace-context trace and span IDs, the HTTP status
  code, exception details and Azure resource metadata, with no per-source
  configuration and, on the common paths, without allocating once the result
  is reused.
authors:
  - family-names: Lindvall
    given-names: Johan
repository-code: "https://github.com/JohanLindvall/enrich"
url: "https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/JohanLindvall/enrich"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - logging
  - log parsing
  - observability
  - OpenTelemetry
  - structured logging
  - logfmt
  - syslog
  - Go
